{"ts":"2026-09-02T18:06:05.839Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"dfa2f27afda31792c334e73d","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-ado-1zuu"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Map typed work item relations onto pm parent and dependency kinds in both directions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Azure DevOps relations are typed rather than free-form: Parent, Child, Related, Duplicate, Predecessor and Successor each carry meaning the pm model already has a home for. Parent and Child map onto pm hierarchy, and the remaining kinds map onto pm dependency kinds. Round-tripping them preserves structure that a flat field-only sync would discard, and it is what lets a project imported from Azure DevOps still answer a pm graph query."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:mapping"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-02T18:06:05.839Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-02T18:06:05.839Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Each relation kind round-trips without loss; a cycle introduced remotely is refused rather than written into the local hierarchy; an unmapped relation kind is reported rather than silently dropped"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ado-g4v1"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"e1bf6666a44ab19c2a7f3940eaa91b0951693486e48c05ffc1d673dce6a20c59","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-12T23:06:33.094Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"79600c52fa552df2e88fa8ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-12T23:06:33.094Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-12T23:06:33.094Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — mapRelations (index.ts line 506) maps all six ADO relation kinds to pm kinds via RELATION_MAP (parent, child, related, duplicate, blocked_by, blocks); unmapped relation kinds are reported in the unmapped array rather than silently dropped, tested in test/ado.test.ts. REMAINS — only the ADO-to-pm read direction is implemented; there is no pm-to-ADO reverse mapping for writes (buildUpdatePatch handles fields only, not relations), so relations do not round-trip. No cycle detection or refusal exists: a cycle introduced remotely would be written into the local hierarchy without refusal. Both missing pieces are required by the acceptance criteria."}]}],"before_hash":"e1bf6666a44ab19c2a7f3940eaa91b0951693486e48c05ffc1d673dce6a20c59","after_hash":"8cfbd7bd70c73d156d23264e9281e50d2d8a29f0cdb16c46bdc4821bf6f5d132","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e649b0a8b40fd42ad57bba116e62041b2472e3cf3b776ad24a65b513bd3f21d1"}
